<title>ISRAEL: Bank Leumi pays Israel government dividend.</title>
<headline>Bank Leumi pays Israel government dividend.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank Leumi on Wednesday presented the government with a 532 million shekel ($156 million) dividend, the Treasury said.</p>
<p>This was in line with a recent Treasury decision that the state-controlled banks must pay the government dividends equivalent to 35 percent of annual profits as well as funds raised from the forced sale of non-banking assets.</p>
<p>Leumi's payment to the government included 162 million shekels from its 1996 profits and 370 million shekels from the sale of assets.</p>
<p>Leumi also paid 120 million shekels to remaining shareholders.</p>
<p>The Treasury said it expected Bank Hapoalim and Israel Discount Bank to present their dividends shortly.</p>
<p>The dividend policy will remain in effect until 1998.</p>
<p>($1 = 3.40 shekels)</p>
</text>
